# The desktop bundle's Hermes features on top of requirements.in (the core both apps share).
# Compiled with requirements.in, the core lock as constraints and overrides.txt:
#   uv pip compile runtime/hermes/requirements.in runtime/hermes/requirements-desktop.in --python-version 3.14
#     --universal --generate-hashes --constraint runtime/hermes/requirements.txt
#     --override runtime/hermes/overrides.txt --output-file runtime/hermes/requirements-desktop.txt
# Left out on purpose: anything that serves a port (fastapi/uvicorn web dashboard, API server, webhook and SMS
# adapters, ACP), provider SDKs (every model call goes through the app's LLM connection), telemetry uploads, the
# Windows Store updaters of Hermes itself, and local voice models.

# Core dependencies of Hermes that requirements.in does not carry.
